<article class="env-remark" id="06HQ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06HQ">Remark <span data-tag="06HQ">90.9.2</span>.</a> Suppose $\mathcal{F}$ is a predeformation category admitting a smooth morphism $\varphi : \mathcal U \to \mathcal{F}$ from a predeformation category $\mathcal{U}$. Then by Lemma <a href="/tag/06HN" data-tag="06HN">90.8.8</a> $\varphi $ is essentially surjective, so by Lemma <a href="/tag/06HM" data-tag="06HM">90.8.7</a> $p: \mathcal{F} \to \mathcal{C}_\Lambda $ is smooth if and only if the composition $\mathcal U \xrightarrow {\varphi } \mathcal{F} \xrightarrow {p} \mathcal{C}_\Lambda $ is smooth, i.e. $\mathcal{F}$ is smooth if and only if $\mathcal{U}$ is smooth. </p>
</article>